      "writtenOn": "2019-02-13T15:21:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I\u0027m reading this right, in this case we do not send a heci response pack to host?\n\nIn my opinion we should always send a response (with error) so that the host driver can log it. If no response, host driver will timeout \u0026 fail with no error log. You may define enum error codes for the status field and share with me to use in host driver.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 85,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "d8c767f8859fd5c430ca9d2a1332ea208b5693ab",
